---
import ProductLayout from '../../layouts/ProductLayout.astro';
---

<ProductLayout 
  title="AstroRescue R1" 
  tagline="Rapid Response for Critical Emergencies"
  productName="AstroRescue R1 Emergency Response Drone"
  productPdf="AstroRescue R1 Emergency Response Drone.docx"
  description="The AstroRescue R1 Emergency Response Drone is purpose-built for rapid deployment in crisis scenarios. Combining high-speed flight capabilities with advanced sensing technology and real-time communication systems, the R1 provides critical situational awareness and response capabilities to emergency services personnel. Ideal for search and rescue missions, disaster assessment, and emergency medical support, it serves as a force multiplier that enhances response efficiency while prioritizing public safety."
>
  <div class="key-features">
    <h2>Key Features</h2>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>Rapid Deployment</h3>
        <p>Designed for immediate launch with minimal setup time, enabling fast response to evolving emergencies.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>Advanced Imaging Suite</h3>
        <p>Multiple camera systems including thermal imaging, night vision, and high-definition optical for comprehensive situational awareness.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>Emergency Payload System</h3>
        <p>Modular attachment system for delivering critical supplies such as emergency medical kits, communication devices, or life-saving equipment.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>Real-Time Communications</h3>
        <p>Secure data transmission with multi-channel communication systems for seamless integration with emergency response networks.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>All-Condition Operation</h3>
        <p>Ruggedized design for reliable performance in adverse weather conditions and challenging environments.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Detailed Specifications</h2>
  
  <h3>Hardware</h3>
  <div class="spec-grid">
    <div class="spec-card">
      <h4>Imaging & Detection</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Multi-Spectrum Camera Array: HD optical, thermal, and low-light/night vision capabilities</li>
        <li>Search-Optimized Sensors: Heat signature detection for locating individuals in challenging environments</li>
        <li>LiDAR: Provides terrain mapping and obstacle detection with centimeter precision</li>
        <li>Audio Sensors: High-sensitivity microphones for detecting calls for help or distress signals</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    
    <div class="spec-card">
      <h4>Propulsion & Mobility</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Speed: Maximum speed of 80 km/h for rapid site access</li>
        <li>Flight Time: Up to 35 minutes with standard battery configuration</li>
        <li>Quick-Change Battery: Hot-swappable power system for extended mission duration</li>
        <li>Wind Resistance: Stable operation in winds up to 65 km/h</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    
    <div class="spec-card">
      <h4>Payload & Construction</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Modular Payload Bay: Configurable for various emergency equipment (2 kg capacity)</li>
        <li>Construction: Impact-resistant composite materials and reinforced frame</li>
        <li>Weather Protection: IP67-rated for dust and water resistance in harsh conditions</li>
        <li>Visibility: High-visibility markings and emergency lighting for night operations</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  
  <h3>Software</h3>
  <div class="spec-grid">
    <div class="spec-card">
      <h4>Emergency Response AI</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Search Pattern Algorithms: Optimized flight paths for various search and rescue scenarios</li>
        <li>Person Detection: AI-powered detection of individuals in distress with low false-positive rate</li>
        <li>Hazard Identification: Automated recognition of dangerous conditions (fires, structural damage, etc.)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    
    <div class="spec-card">
      <h4>Communications</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Redundant Data Links: Multiple communication channels ensuring uninterrupted connectivity</li>
        <li>Emergency Services Integration: Compatible with standard emergency response communication protocols</li>
        <li>Broadcast Capability: Equipped with loudspeaker for direct communication with individuals in distress</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    
    <div class="spec-card">
      <h4>User Interface</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Emergency Response Console: Specialized dashboard with simplified crisis management controls</li>
        <li>Mobile Command Center: Tablet-based interface for field operations with intuitive controls</li>
        <li>Real-Time Mapping: Dynamic situation mapping with integrated GIS for coordinated response</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  
  <h3>Operational Parameters</h3>
  <div class="spec-grid">
    <div class="spec-card">
      <h4>Deployment & Range</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Launch Time: Under 60 seconds from case to active flight</li>
        <li>Operational Range: Up to 10 km from command center with standard configuration</li>
        <li>Deployment Method: Rapid-deploy carrying case with integrated launch platform</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    
    <div class="spec-card">
      <h4>Environmental Adaptation</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Temperature Range: -20°C to 50°C operational capability</li>
        <li>Adverse Weather: Effective in rain, snow, and dusty conditions with appropriate flight adjustments</li>
        <li>Lighting Conditions: Full operational capability in daylight, twilight, and night operations</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    
    <div class="spec-card">
      <h4>Safety & Compliance</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Fail-Safe Systems: Multiple redundancies for critical flight systems</li>
        <li>Emergency Override: Priority flight clearance integration with air traffic control</li>
        <li>Visual/Audio Warnings: High-visibility strobes and sirens for public safety awareness</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Use Cases & Integration</h2>
  
  <h3>Emergency Response Scenarios</h3>
  <div class="use-case">
    <p><strong>Search and Rescue:</strong> Rapidly locating missing persons or individuals in distress using thermal imaging and AI-powered detection in various terrains.</p>
    <p><strong>Disaster Assessment:</strong> Immediate aerial surveying of disaster areas to assess damage, identify hazards, and prioritize response resources.</p>
    <p><strong>Medical Emergencies:</strong> Delivering critical medical supplies to remote locations or providing visual telemedicine support to first responders.</p>
  </div>
  
  <h3>Public Safety Support</h3>
  <div class="use-case">
    <p><strong>Fire Response:</strong> Providing aerial thermal mapping of fire scenes to direct firefighting efforts and identify hotspots.</p>
    <p><strong>Hazardous Material Incidents:</strong> Remote assessment of chemical spills or dangerous materials without exposing personnel to risks.</p>
    <p><strong>Mass Casualty Support:</strong> Enhancing situational awareness and coordination during large-scale incidents by providing real-time aerial intelligence.</p>
  </div>
  
  <h3>Integration Diagram</h3>
  <div class="integration-diagram">
    <pre>
{`
 +-------------------------+         +-------------------------+         +-------------------------+
  |  AstroRescue R1 Drone   |  --->   |  Emergency Response     |  --->   |  Command & Control      |
  |  - Sensors & Equipment  |         |  Mobile Command Unit    |         |  Emergency Services     |
  +-------------------------+         +-------------------------+         +-------------------------+
           |      ^                             |      ^
           |      |                             |      |
           v      |                             v      |
  +------------------+               +-------------------------+
  | Communication &  | <-----------  | Notification & Alert    |
  | Broadcast System |               | Priority Dispatch       |
  +------------------+               +-------------------------+
`}
    </pre>
  </div>

  <h2>Setup and Configuration</h2>
  
  <h3>Rapid Deployment Process</h3>
  <div class="setup-steps">
    <p><strong>Pre-mission Check:</strong> Automated system diagnostics performed during transit to incident location.</p>
    <p><strong>Deployment:</strong> Quick-release from transport case with immediate system initialization.</p>
    <p><strong>Mission Configuration:</strong> Rapid selection of preprogrammed mission profiles based on emergency type.</p>
  </div>
  
  <h3>Field Operations</h3>
  <div class="setup-steps">
    <p><strong>Command Interface:</strong> Rugged tablet with simplified emergency controls for field use.</p>
    <p><strong>Real-Time Adjustment:</strong> On-the-fly mission parameter updates as emergency conditions evolve.</p>
    <p><strong>Multi-Agency Coordination:</strong> Secure data sharing with authorized emergency service partners.</p>
  </div>
  
  <h3>System Integration</h3>
  <div class="setup-steps">
    <p><strong>Emergency Services:</strong> Direct integration with dispatch systems for seamless resource coordination.</p>
    <p><strong>Medical Support:</strong> Compatible with telemedicine platforms for remote medical assessment.</p>
    <p><strong>Data Management:</strong> Secure incident recording and documentation for after-action review.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Support & Troubleshooting</h2>
  
  <h3>Emergency Support</h3>
  <div class="faq-list">
    <div class="faq-item">
      <p class="faq-question">Q1: What is the deployment procedure during critical incidents?</p>
      <p>A1: The AstroRescue R1 uses a one-touch deployment system - open the transport case, press the emergency launch button, and the drone will automatically initialize, perform system checks, and launch within 60 seconds.</p>
    </div>
    
    <div class="faq-item">
      <p class="faq-question">Q2: How does the system handle communication failures?</p>
      <p>A2: Multiple redundant communication systems automatically switch between cellular, radio frequency, and satellite connections. If all links fail, the drone executes predefined emergency protocols based on mission type.</p>
    </div>
    
    <div class="faq-item">
      <p class="faq-question">Q3: Can the drone operate in smoke or poor visibility?</p>
      <p>A3: Yes, the AstroRescue R1 is equipped with thermal imaging and specialized sensors designed to function in smoke, fog, and low-light conditions, maintaining operational capability where traditional visibility is compromised.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  
  <h3>Emergency Contact Information</h3>
  <div class="contact-info">
    <p><strong>24/7 Emergency Hotline:</strong> +1-800-ASTR-911 (278-7911)</p>
    <p><strong>Priority Support Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:emergency@astroflyrobotics.com">emergency@astroflyrobotics.com</a></p>
    <p><strong>Emergency Response Team:</strong> Available for immediate deployment support via the Mobile Command Unit</p>
    <p><strong>Support Portal:</strong> <a href="https://www.astroflyrobotics.com/emergency-support" target="_blank">www.astroflyrobotics.com/emergency-support</a></p>
  </div>
</ProductLayout>

<style>
  .feature-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(300px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }
  
  .feature-card {
    background-color: white;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-lg);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-accent);
  }
  
  .use-case {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }
  
  .use-case p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }
  
  .use-case strong {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  
  .setup-steps {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }
  
  .setup-steps p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }
  
  .setup-steps strong {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  
  .integration-diagram pre {
    font-family: monospace;
    white-space: pre;
    overflow-x: auto;
    padding: var(--space-md);
    background-color: #f8f9fa;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }
  
  .contact-info p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }
</style>
